mpegaudiodec: fail on packets too large for the bit reader (CVE-2026-125072)

mp_decode_frame() set up its bit reader with init_get_bits() and a bit count of
(buf_size - HEADER_SIZE) * 8. A packet too large for that count left the reader
with a NULL buffer that the layer decoders then read through. The patch uses
init_get_bits8() and returns its error.

Backport of FFmpeg master 0b007e0634de5b4424b9993c95a6c1c50de0115b (PR 25696, merged 2026-11-03), not in n9.0.2.
Ported by hand: n9.0.2 reads s->error_protection where master reads
s->hdr.error_protection; the change itself is the same three lines.

diff --git a/libavcodec/mpegaudiodec_template.c b/libavcodec/mpegaudiodec_template.c
--- a/libavcodec/mpegaudiodec_template.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mpegaudiodec_template.c
@@ -1474,7 +1474,9 @@ static int mp_decode_frame(MPADecodeContext *s, OUT_INT **samples,
     int i, nb_frames, ch, ret;
     OUT_INT *samples_ptr;
 
-    init_get_bits(&s->gb, buf + HEADER_SIZE, (buf_size - HEADER_SIZE) * 8);
+    ret = init_get_bits8(&s->gb, buf + HEADER_SIZE, buf_size - HEADER_SIZE);
+    if (ret < 0)
+        return ret;
     if (s->error_protection)
         s->crc = get_bits(&s->gb, 16);
 
